# Claims waived in writing — Rule 27 (bin/gates/guards/docs-claims-guard.sh).
#
# One path per line. A path belongs here when a document names it ON PURPOSE and the repo does
# not ship it, because it is not the repo's to ship. Everything else must resolve.
#
# config/agents.yaml — the OPERATOR'S own file, written into the home by the install (the repo
# ships config/agents.yaml.example, which is the template those documents are describing).
config/agents.yaml
# .agents/skills-local/ — the per-machine skill shelf, gitignored by design: it is the one shelf
# that must never travel, and a document naming it is describing a shelf that exists only here.
.agents/skills-local/
# apps/odrerir/public/livehall.json — generated at runtime from the hall's own state; the repo
# ships the generator, not its output.
apps/odrerir/public/livehall.json
config/cron.yaml
config/tailscale-sync.yaml
